      "SARAH: Even my roommate and I. We have more of a truce than a friendship.\nCARLA: Too loud?\nSARAH: Getting some water.\nSARAH: Carla wonders why I never say anything. Most people would kill for a roommate like me. I think she assumes I'm scolding her for being too lo…",
      "GAYLE: We just talked to Carla. Apparently, you got an important call this morning. Sarah can't believe her ears. This is definitely not how she wa…\nSARAH: I can explain...\nGAYLE: You did it, sweetheart. Sarah is completely confused by these words.",
      "GAYLE: Hi.\nSARAH: Got a minute?\nGAYLE: Have a seat.\nSARAH: You were probably wondering why I came home like I did...",
      "SARAH: I came by to-- Sarah stops abruptly. How is she supposed to do this? Blurt out “Can you forgive me?\"? Lorraine looks up, almost as if she he…\nSARAH: That's beautiful.\nLORRAINE: Is that why you came over? You want something restored? Sarah is startled by Lorraine's voice. She grabs onto the lifeline Lorraine has inad…\nSARAH: Maybe.",
      "SARAH: Hello?\nLORRAINE: I just realized that I was being very rude.\nSARAH: No ... it was me. I don't know what I was thinking just barging in like that. I had no right--\nLORRAINE: If you want to come by tomorrow, I can show you some samples and help you figure out what you want."
    ]
